      <!-- Section 4: Ergonomics & RSI Prevention -->
      <section class="space-y-6">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-amber-50 dark:bg-amber-950/40 border border-amber-200 dark:border-amber-800 text-xs font-mono font-semibold text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-400 uppercase tracking-wider">
          Section 4 · Ergonomics & Physical Health
        </div>
        <h2 class="font-heading font-extrabold text-3xl sm:text-4xl text-zinc-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight">
          Ergonomics, Wrist Neutrality & RSI / Carpal Tunnel Prevention
        </h2>
        <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed">
          High-volume typing subjects the fingers, wrists, and forearms to thousands of repetitive micro-trauma cycles per hour. Poor biomechanical form frequently leads to <strong>Repetitive Strain Injury (RSI)</strong>, Carpal Tunnel Syndrome (median nerve entrapment), and de Quervain's tenosynovitis.
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 pt-2">
          <div class="p-6 rounded-3xl bg-zinc-50 dark:bg-zinc-900 border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 space-y-2">
            <div class="mb-1 text-amber-500"><svg class="w-7 h-7" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" /><polygon points="16.24 7.76 14.12 14.12 7.76 16.24 9.88 9.88 16.24 7.76" /></svg></div>
            <h3 class="font-heading font-bold text-lg text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">Neutral Wrist Posture</h3>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
              Keep wrists straight and floating. Never rest your wrists on hard desk surfaces while typing; wrist rests are meant for resting <em>between</em> typing bursts, not during.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-6 rounded-3xl bg-zinc-50 dark:bg-zinc-900 border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 space-y-2">
            <div class="mb-1 text-amber-500"><svg class="w-7 h-7" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><rect x="2" y="6" width="20" height="12" rx="2" /><path d="M6 10h.01M10 10h.01M14 10h.01M18 10h.01M6 14h.01M18 14h.01M9 14h6" /></svg></div>
            <h3 class="font-heading font-bold text-lg text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">Flat / Negative Tilt</h3>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
              Avoid using the flip-out feet on keyboards. Angling the keyboard upward forces wrists into dorsiflexion, compressing the carpal tunnel. Keep keyboards flat or slightly negatively tilted.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-6 rounded-3xl bg-zinc-50 dark:bg-zinc-900 border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 space-y-2">
            <div class="mb-1 text-amber-500"><svg class="w-7 h-7" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M20 9V6a2 2 0 0 0-2-2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v3" /><path d="M2 16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h16a2 2 0 0 0 2-2v-5a2 2 0 0 0-4 0v2H6v-2a2 2 0 0 0-4 0Z" /><path d="M4 18v2" /><path d="M20 18v2" /></svg></div>
            <h3 class="font-heading font-bold text-lg text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">90° Elbow Angle</h3>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
              Adjust chair height so forearms rest parallel to the floor with relaxed shoulders. Keep elbows close to your torso at a comfortable 90° to 105° open angle.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 5: Deliberate Practice Protocols -->
      <section class="space-y-6">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-amber-50 dark:bg-amber-950/40 border border-amber-200 dark:border-amber-800 text-xs font-mono font-semibold text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-400 uppercase tracking-wider">
          Section 5 · Skill Acquisition
        </div>
        <h2 class="font-heading font-extrabold text-3xl sm:text-4xl text-zinc-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight">
          Deliberate Practice Protocols to Break the 100+ WPM Plateau
        </h2>
        <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed">
          Simply typing emails and documents for years rarely increases typing speed beyond 60 WPM. To break through speed plateaus, adopt deliberate practice methodologies:
        </p>

        <ul class="space-y-4 text-base text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="font-mono font-bold text-amber-500 text-lg">01.</span>
            <div>
              <strong class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">The 98% Accuracy Rule:</strong> Speed is a byproduct of accuracy. If your accuracy dips below 96%, slow down your raw speed by 15% until accuracy returns to 98%+. High accuracy reinforces clean neural pathways without erroneous motor stutter.
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="font-mono font-bold text-amber-500 text-lg">02.</span>
            <div>
              <strong class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">Burst Sprint Training:</strong> Conduct five 15-second max-velocity sprints daily. Short sprints train your motor cortex to execute multi-finger chords at speeds exceeding your normal 60-second endurance threshold.
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="font-mono font-bold text-amber-500 text-lg">03.</span>
            <div>
              <strong class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">N-Gram Targeted Drills:</strong> Use error heatmaps to isolate recurring finger confusion pairs (e.g. <code>b</code> vs <code>v</code> with left index, or <code>p</code> with weak right pinky). Run deliberate 5-minute drills isolating those specific trigrams.
            </div>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 6: FAQ Accordion -->
